WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:04.080
In 2019, Game of Thrones ended.

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:09.240
Game of Thrones is why Alt Shift X took off
in the first place – in 2014, our first

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:15.150
Thrones video explored R+L=J, the granddaddy
of Thrones theories.

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:19.840
That video came out after Game of Thrones
Season 4 – arguably the high point of the

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:25.090
series – and rode off Thrones’ popularity
to start an audience for Alt Shift X.

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:30.740
In 2015, we started this Patreon, which makes
it possible to make more videos, without sacrificing

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:36.250
quality – Alt Shift X is about deep research,
clear explanations, and nice visuals, with

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:39.100
no clickbait, and no bullshit.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:44.199
With your support over the last 5 years, we
developed a style, hit one million subscribers,

00:00:44.199 --> 00:00:49.339
and made a hundred videos – we covered Westworld,
The Expanse, Game of Bones…

00:00:49.339 --> 00:00:55.030
But mostly Game of Thrones and A Song of Ice
and Fire – Cersei, Rhaegar, Bloodraven,

00:00:55.030 --> 00:01:00.049
Stark mysteries, and videos on every Thrones
episode since Season 6.

00:01:00.049 --> 00:01:03.699
Now that Thrones is over, Alt Shift X will
keep evolving.

00:01:03.699 --> 00:01:08.340
We’ll make more videos on the Game of Thrones
books, and we’ll cover more new series.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:13.420
And this is only possible with the support
of our Patrons, so we held a Patron survey

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:16.170
to decide which series to cover.

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:20.189
Patrons want more videos about the Game of
Thrones books – so of course, we’ll make

00:01:20.189 --> 00:01:26.750
lots more ASOIAF videos, like the recent Dayne
video and an upcoming Pink Letter video.

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:32.530
We’ll hold more votes on Patreon to choose
future topics like Euron’s eldritch apocalypse,

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:39.299
the Dorne plot, Hardhome, the Blackfyres – there’s
lots more lore, theories and analysis to cover.

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:43.920
There’s also the possibility that the long-awaited
Winds of Winter will come.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:49.579
George Martin suggested that Winds will be
out by July 2020, for what that’s worth.

00:01:49.579 --> 00:01:55.079
When and if Winds comes, we’ll cover it
with recap videos, livestreams, breakdowns

00:01:55.079 --> 00:01:57.219
– it’ll be fucking nuts.

00:01:57.219 --> 00:02:02.509
There are also GOT prequel shows coming, but
they’re pretty far off, and in the meantime,

00:02:02.509 --> 00:02:04.909
there are other cool shows to cover.

00:02:04.909 --> 00:02:08.509
The second most popular series in the survey
is Westworld.

00:02:08.509 --> 00:02:16.170
Westworld is ambitious and messy and lavish
and smart and dumb and a joy to watch.

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:21.480
Westworld Season 3 seems to focus on Dolores,
Bernard and Jesse Pinkman, and will apparently

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:25.400
be more focussed than the bombastic Season
2.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:29.069
So we’ll cover Season 3, probably with weekly
videos.

00:02:29.069 --> 00:02:33.480
If you’re interested, Patreon supporters
can watch the uncensored version of the Alt

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:37.739
Schwift X Westworld Rant video that’s blocked
on YouTube.

00:02:37.739 --> 00:02:42.400
The third most popular series in the survey
is Lord of the Rings – Amazon is spending

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:47.180
a bajillion dollars on an upcoming LOTR TV
show, and it might be worth making videos

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:52.330
about, if it’s complex, and draws from the
books, and is… good.

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:57.670
But either way, it’ll be an excuse to talk
about the original story that defined modern

00:02:57.670 --> 00:02:59.020
fantasy.

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:04.409
The fourth most popular series is Watchmen
– our Watchmen 2019 video will be out very

00:03:04.409 --> 00:03:05.409
soon.

00:03:05.409 --> 00:03:09.819
And we can totally do more Watchmen videos
– like maybe one on the visual storytelling

00:03:09.819 --> 00:03:12.709
and symbolism of the original comic.

00:03:12.709 --> 00:03:18.470
Also popular in the survey was Witcher, The
Expanse, Dune, His Dark Materials, and real-world

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:20.500
sciency history stuff.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:25.650
Witcher we haven’t watched yet, but it might
be worth some videos before Season 2.

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:30.360
We can definitely do more Expanse, maybe a
video about the protomolecule or something

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:32.140
before Season 5.

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:37.879
Dune has a movie coming out in 2020, so now’s
a great time to talk about spice and sand

00:03:37.879 --> 00:03:38.900
worms.

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:43.500
For His Dark Materials, we could do a video
about Dust and the story’s big ideas in

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:45.480
Book 1 / Season 1.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:50.959
As for science / history / edu stuff, we’ve
got ideas for some cool videos about the real

00:03:50.959 --> 00:03:56.819
world – Alt Shift X began with videos about
science and philosophy, a long time ago.

00:03:56.819 --> 00:04:03.519
So that’s the rough plan for Alt Shift X
in 2020 – more ASOIAF, more Westworld, probably

00:04:03.519 --> 00:04:09.420
Expanse Dune His Dark Materials edu, Lord
of the Rings when it’s done, and whatever

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:13.969
other cool stories come up – comment below
if you’ve got more ideas.

00:04:13.969 --> 00:04:19.140
We can’t do everything – but we’ll hold
votes on Patreon, see which shows are good,

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:21.660
and make some kickass videos.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:29.660
For votes, updates, livestreams, and Patron-only
content, join the Patreon at patreon.com/AltShiftX.

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:34.280
There are Patron-only videos about symbolism
in Watchmen, and His Dark Materials, and the

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:37.290
uncensored Westworld Rant, and more.

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:41.470
So thank you for watching, and thanks to the
Patrons for your support.

00:04:41.470 --> 00:04:46.450
Thank you for the last five years, for sticking
with Alt Shift X through the highs and the

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:48.630
lows of Game of Thrones.

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:51.150
Here’s to five years more.

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:57.500
Oh and I swear we’ll do that Alt Shift Podcast
one day, it’s gonna happen, uh shoutout

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:03.810
to Alt Schwift X, Alt Shift ZZZ, Random Article,
Internet Historian, VaatiVidya, and all those

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:05.410
other Alt Shift X side-channels.

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:06.080
Cheers.

